# tests/dataflow_stream.rs::data_stream_limits_and_typed_errors at tests/dataflow_stream.rs:53; converter c4189f521f54bea78e49f62cb127d50ad22ac3e0
# PENDING-SAME-HEAD; no captures blessed. Source and .out follow current law:
# - `writer :=` / `reader :=` and plain `writer.write|flush|finish`, `stream.next(reader)`:
#   D-BIND1 (syntax-decisions.md:21-22; spec.md:1169-1170) and D-CALLSITE-MARK2
#   (memory marks live in signatures only); `next` is the module function `stream.next(stream)`
#   (core-library.md:3106), so the source imports `core.data.stream as stream`.
# - .out line 2: `data.query(stream)` carries the reader's limits
#   (core-library.md `query(stream)`), so the reader's max_groups=1 refuses
#   the 2 groups left after `next` (as tooling/data_hostile).
# - The build names FS.Read,FS.Write on the command line; they are allowed
#   without the flag too (every effect is allowed), and the flag only acknowledges them.
fixture: data_stream_limits_and_typed_errors.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
write: run.jet data_stream_limits_and_typed_errors.source.template
step: jet build --allow=FS.Read,FS.Write run.jet
exit: 0
step aot: built
exit: any # original predicate: only stdout asserted, no runtime status assertion
stdout: = data_stream_limits_and_typed_errors.out
